{"event_type":"tool_call","timestamp":"2026-06-17T20:15:00.166865Z","session_id":"2026-05-15_155415","project_id":"opencode_cc_mem","source":"magnolia-run","tool":"shell","args_summary":"bash -c WD=projects/hsc70_new/runs/2026-06-17_mmgbsa_analysis/RKALQ_5mer\n\n# Receptor goes from 1 to 646, peptide from 1 to 5 in prmtop\n# In prmtop, the receptor would be residues 1-646 and peptide 647-651\n# But wait - tleap renumbers the complex. Let me check.\n\n# Actually, looking at the existing KFERQ analysis:\n# RRES 1 646 means receptor residues 1-646 in the complex prmtop\n# LRES 647 651 means peptide residues 647-651\n\n# For RKALQ: receptor should still be ~646 residues, peptide adds 5 = 651 total\n# But the receptor PDB may have fewer residues than the full model.\n# Let me check from the prmtop\n\npython3 -c \"\nimport parmed as pmd\nc = pmd.load_file('projects/hsc70_new/runs/2026-06-17_mmgbsa_analysis/RKALQ_5mer/complex.prmtop')\nprint(f'Total residues: {len(c.residues)}')\nfor i, r in enumerate(c.residues):\n    if i < 5 or i > len(c.residues) - 8:\n        print(f'  Res {i+1}: {r.name} (chain {r.chain})')\n\" 2>&1 | head -20"}
