{"event_type":"tool_call","timestamp":"2026-06-18T12:49:16.410686Z","session_id":"2026-05-15_155415","project_id":"opencode_cc_mem","source":"magnolia-run","tool":"shell","args_summary":"bash -c set -e\ncd projects/hsc70_new/runs/2026-06-17_mmgbsa_analysis/TGFMALQ_7mer\n\n# Count receptor residues from the complex prmtop\necho \"=== Checking topology residue count ===\"\nconda run -n ambertools python3 -c \"\nwith open('complex.prmtop', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n# Find POINTERS section to get NATOM, NRES\nimport re\n# The POINTERS section has NATOM, NTYPES, NBONH, etc.\n# In Amber prmtop, the first line of %FLAG POINTERS has key values\n# Actually, let me just count from the RESIDUE_LABEL section\nlabels = re.findall(r'%FLAG RESIDUE_LABEL.*?%FORMAT.*?\\n(.*?)%FLAG', content, re.DOTALL)\nif labels:\n    label_text = labels[0].strip()\n    res_names = label_text.split()\n    print(f'Total residues in complex: {len(res_names)}')\n    # Print last 10\n    for i, name in enumerate(res_names[-10:]):\n        print(f'  Res {len(res_names)-10+i+1}: {name}')\n\" 2>&1\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Creating sander input ===\"\n# Peptide is residues 647-653 (7 residues after receptor 646)\ncat > sander_decomp.mdin << 'EOF'\nPer-residue energy decomposition\n &cntrl\n  ntb=0, nsnb=99999, cut=999.0, imin=5,\n  ncyc=0, igb=5, saltcon=0.15, gbsa=2,\n  surften=0.0072, extdiel=80.0,\n  idecomp=2,\n /\nResidues considered as REC\nRRES 1 646\nEND\nResidues considered as LIG\nLRES 647 653\nEND\nResidues to print\nRES 647 647\nRES 648 648\nRES 649 649\nRES 650 650\nRES 651 651\nRES 652 652\nRES 653 653\nEND\nEND\nEOF\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Running sander idecomp ===\"\nconda run -n ambertools sander -O -i sander_decomp.mdin \\\n  -p complex.prmtop \\\n  -c complex.rst7 \\\n  -o sander_decomp.out \\\n  -r restrt \\\n  -inf sander_decomp.mdinfo 2>&1 | tail -10"}
