{"event_type":"tool_call","timestamp":"2026-06-18T12:49:35.803041Z","session_id":"2026-05-15_155415","project_id":"opencode_cc_mem","source":"magnolia-run","tool":"shell","args_summary":"bash -c # Check if sander actually produced output despite the inptraj error\ncd projects/hsc70_new/runs/2026-06-17_mmgbsa_analysis/TGFMALQ_7mer\necho \"=== Output files ===\"\nls -la sander_decomp.out restrt 2>/dev/null\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Sander output tail ===\"\ntail -20 sander_decomp.out 2>/dev/null\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Check for DECOMP section ===\"\ngrep -c 'DECOMP\\|TDC\\|VDW' sander_decomp.out 2>/dev/null\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Let me fix: need mdcrd trajectory for sander ===\"\n# Create the mdcrd from the rst7\ncat > cpptraj2.in << 'EOF'\nparm complex.prmtop\ntrajin complex.rst7\ntrajout inptraj mdcrd\ngo\nEOF\nconda run -n ambertools cpptraj -i cpptraj2.in 2>&1 | tail -3\n\n# Now run sander again \u2014 but use the mdcrd as input\n# Actually with imin=5, sander reads from -c (rst7) not from inptraj\n# The inptraj error for idecomp is about reading the trajectory for decomposition\n# Let me check the RKALQ output more carefully\necho \"\"\necho \"=== How did RKALQ handle this? ===\"\ngrep -A3 'inptraj\\|FILE' ../../2026-06-17_mmgbsa_analysis/RKALQ_5mer/sander.log 2>/dev/null"}
