{"event_type":"tool_call","timestamp":"2026-06-21T09:52:36.003860Z","session_id":"2026-05-15_155415","project_id":"opencode_cc_mem","source":"magnolia-run","tool":"shell","args_summary":"bash -c cd /home/tjiang/repos/project_magnolia/opencode_cc_mem/projects/studium/studium && echo \"=== COMMIT 1: rebuild stale m3 ZIP ===\" && git add fixtures/m3/demo-metabolomics-bundle.zip && git commit -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(eval): rebuild stale m3 fixture ZIP to schema 1.4\n\nThe committed fixtures/m3/demo-metabolomics-bundle.zip was last built\n2026-05-08 with schema_version: \"1.0\". The source\nfixtures/m3/demo-metabolomics/lesson.json was later migrated to \"1.4\"\n(the current LessonBundle schema requirement) but the ZIP was never\nrebuilt, so `eval/run_eval.py --smoke` failed immediately with a\nZodError on schema_version + missing required fields.\n\nRebuilt via the canonical `bash fixtures/m3/demo-metabolomics/build.sh`.\nThe other committed bundles (atomistique-l1, m6/demo-atomistique) were\nalready at 1.4 and need no changes.\nEOF\necho \"exit=$?\"; echo \"=== COMMIT 2: .env loader ===\" && git add .gitignore .env.example eval/harness/env.py && git commit -F - <<'EOF'\nfeat(eval): dependency-free .env loader for harness config\n\nAdds eval/harness/env.py (~95 LOC, no python-dotenv dependency \u2014 the\nharness values thin seams). Search order: $STUDIUM_ENV_FILE,\n<repo>/.env, ~/.config/studium/.env. Real env vars override file\nvalues, so ad-hoc `KEY=val cmd` invocations still win.\n\n- Keys named *KEY/*SECRET/*TOKEN are masked in --env-verbose output.\n- .gitignore: ignore .env* but whitelist .env.example.\n- .env.example: documents DeepSeek, GLM/Zhipu (coding plan + standard\n  API), OpenRouter, etc., plus cross-provider STUDIUM_AUDIT_LLM_*\n  variables for breaking the same-model-authored-and-audited bias.\n\nrun_eval.py loads .env at startup (before harness module imports) so\nany os.getenv() in author/audit/grounding sees file-provided values.\nEOF\necho \"exit=$?\"; echo \"=== COMMIT 3: multi-provider LLM bridge ===\" && git add eval/harness/llm.py eval/harness/author.py eval/harness/audit.py eval/run_eval.py && git commit -F - <<'EOF'\nfeat(eval): multi-provider LLM bridge (OpenAI-compat + Anthropic-compat)\n\nAdds two new LLM backend classes to eval/harness/llm.py, both duck-\ntype-compatible with ClaudeCli (same complete() / complete_json()\ninterface):\n\n- OpenAICompletionsLLM: any /v1/chat/completions endpoint. Works with\n  DeepSeek, GLM/Zhipu standard API, OpenAI, OpenRouter, Together,\n  vLLM, Ollama, LiteLLM proxy.\n- AnthropicMessagesLLM: native Anthropic Messages API. Required for\n  keys that only work at Anthropic-compat endpoints \u2014 notably the GLM\n  coding plan, which authenticates at api.z.ai/api/anthropic but\n  returns \"429 Insufficient balance\" at /api/paas/v4.\n\nProtocol auto-detected from BASE_URL substring \"anthropic\", or forced\nvia STUDIUM_LLM_PROTOCOL=openai|anthropic.\n\nNew --author openai choice in run_eval.py (keeps --author claude and\n--author deterministic for backward compat). Auditor (--audit-llm)\nauto-detects the same backend; cross-provider auditing supported via\nSTUDIUM_AUDIT_LLM_* env (different provider than author \u2014 breaks the\n\"same model authored AND audited\" shared-blind-spot bias).\n\nDefensive: detects \"HTTP 200 with error envelope\" (some proxies do\nthis) and raises a clear LLMError pointing at the fix (e.g. missing\n/v1 path segment) instead of silently returning empty content.\nEOF\necho \"exit=$?\"; echo \"=== verify the 3 commits landed cleanly ===\" && git log --oneline -5; echo \"=== final tree state (should be clean) ===\" && git status --short"}
