{"event_type":"tool_call","timestamp":"2026-06-21T16:08:30.715664Z","session_id":"2026-05-15_155415","project_id":"opencode_cc_mem","source":"magnolia-run","tool":"shell","args_summary":"bash -c cd /home/tjiang/repos/project_magnolia/opencode_cc_mem/projects/studium/studium && git add .env.example apps/student-runtime/package.json apps/student-runtime/src-tauri/Cargo.lock apps/student-runtime/src-tauri/Cargo.toml apps/student-runtime/src-tauri/capabilities/default.json apps/student-runtime/src-tauri/src/keystore.rs apps/student-runtime/src-tauri/src/lib.rs apps/student-runtime/src/components/scenes/AICritiqueScene.tsx apps/student-runtime/src/views/LessonPlayer.tsx apps/student-runtime/src/views/LibraryScreen.tsx eval/harness/author.py pnpm-lock.yaml && git commit -F - <<'EOF'\nfeat(student-runtime): make the GUI work end-to-end + Tauri .env loader\n\nThe student-runtime Tauri app was demo-grade \u2014 hardcoded single bundle\npath, no way to switch courses, no schema interop with the Python\nbundler, and panicked on WSL2 where the system keyring is non-functional.\nThis commit makes the app actually playable.\n\nLibrary + bundle loading\n- LibraryScreen: replaced hardcoded demo card with native file picker\n  via tauri-plugin-dialog. The user picks any .zip on disk; the path\n  is passed via the URL query string (?path=...).\n- LessonPlayer: reads bundle path from ?path= URL param (with a\n  default fallback for legacy deep-links). Added explicit error UI\n  for failed loads \u2014 no more silent infinite \"Chargement de la le\u00e7on\u2026\".\n- LessonPlayer: JSON.parse the Rust load_bundle result before Zod\n  (Rust returns the bundle as a JSON string).\n- LessonPlayer: strip null values via JSON reviver before Zod \u2014 the\n  Python bundler emits null for unused optional fields (render_assets,\n  evidence, image_path, ...) but the TS schema declares those as\n  .optional() (absent/undefined), not .nullable(). Without this, every\n  authored bundle fails Zod validation at scene-load time.\n\nAICritiqueScene offline fallback\n- Default POSTs to localhost:8002 (scene-synth critique-eval). When\n  scene-synth isn't running, fetch fails with \"Load failed\" and blocks\n  scene progression. Added graceful fallback to the local\n  matchClaimsAgainstCritique heuristic (same logic the eval harness's\n  StubCritiqueEvaluator uses offline). The user sees \"(Mode hors-ligne\n  \u2014 service d'\u00e9valuation LLM injoignable...)\" + a recall-based score,\n  and can continue. Also fixed a downstream bug: the fallback assumed\n  MatchResult.planted_errors was an array; it's a number (count).\n\nTauri .env loader (single source of truth with Python harness)\n- lib.rs::load_dotenv() walks up from CWD to find a .env file, same\n  logic as eval/harness/env.py. Existing env vars are NOT overridden.\n- Adds dotenvy = \"0.15\" Rust dep. The Tauri runtime now reads the same\n  .env as the Python harness \u2014 STUDIUM_LLM_*, STUDIUM_AUDIT_LLM_*,\n  STUDIUM_PERSPICACITE_*, STUDIUM_KEYRING_FALLBACK flow into both\n  runtimes uniformly.\n\nWSL2 keyring fallback (STUDIUM_KEYRING_FALLBACK=derived)\n- On WSL2 without gnome-keyring-daemon, the keyring crate silently\n  \"succeeds\" at storing but doesn't persist \u2192 each session generates\n  a fresh random SQLCipher key \u2192 can't decrypt the previous session's\n  DB \u2192 panic at startup (\"file is not a database\", SQLITE_NOTADB).\n- keystore.rs: when STUDIUM_KEYRING_FALLBACK=derived is set, bypass\n  the system keyring and derive the SQLCipher key deterministically\n  from SHA-256(app-salt || USER || home_dir). Stable across sessions,\n  no keyring needed. Trade-off: anyone with the user's login can\n  derive the key. Fine for a single-user research-prototype machine.\n\nEval harness: STUDIUM_AUTHOR_BODY_MAX_CHARS env override\n- author.py:_claude_content hardcodes body[:9000], which truncated\n  65% of a 26K-char chapter. Made the limit env-overridable (default\n  9000 preserved).\n\nLockfiles refreshed for the new deps.\nEOF\necho \"exit=$?\"; echo \"=== verify ===\" && git log --oneline -4; echo \"=== tree clean? ===\" && git status --short"}
