{"event_type":"tool_call","timestamp":"2026-06-23T14:11:23.496070Z","session_id":"2026-05-15_155415","project_id":"opencode_cc_mem","source":"magnolia-run","tool":"shell","args_summary":"bash -c cat > /tmp/hsc70_retrieval_report.md << 'REPORT_EOF'\n# Hsc70_new Project: Retrieval-and-Reuse Audit\n\n**Date**: 2026-06-23  \n**Database**: `/home/tjiang/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`  \n**Sessions analyzed**: 20 (June 11 \u2013 June 23)  \n**Total memory retrieval calls**: 53 (16 get_context + 31 search + 2 select_relevant + 4 search_errors)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Summary\n\nMagnolia **does retrieve** past learnings across session boundaries, and **does sometimes act** on them. However, the system has **significant bugs** that reduce retrieval effectiveness. The overall signal is: the infrastructure is there but the retrieval pipeline has holes.\n\n---\n\n## 2. `memory_get_context` \u2014 16 calls\n\n### What it returns\nEach call returns a text blob containing:\n1. **Project Goal** (from `boot-context.md`) \u2014 always present\n2. **Session Observations** \u2014 numbered entries (\"Observation 1/2/3\") from prior session handovers\n3. **Project-tier entry titles** \u2014 from `.magnolia/entries/` and staging\n\n### Content stats\n| Session | Date | Content chars | Observations | Project entries found |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ses_14a8d1 (June 11) | earliest | 20,546 | 4 | 4 title matches |\n| ses_1456d0 (June 12) | | 12,488 / 9,566 | 1 each | 4-5 |\n| ses_13fc23 (June 13) | | 16,853 / 6,704 | 1-2 each | 4-5 |\n| ses_134c7b (June 15) | | 0* | 0 | 0 |\n| ses_130e4d (June 16) | | 19,969 | 0 | 30+ entry filename matches |\n| ses_12b819 (June 17) | | 0 / 0 / 20,444 / 24,666 | 0-2 each | 4-5 entry titles each |\n| ses_12a464 (June 17) | | 23,050 | 1 | 4 |\n| ses_12a315 (June 17) | | 21,435 | 1 | 4 |\n| ses_120fa9 (June 19) | | 25,968 | 2 | 7 |\n| ses_10bc31 (June 23) | | 15,316 | 2 | 4 |\n| ses_11186e (June 22) | | 0* | 0 | 0 |\n\n`*` = result key wrapped in `{\"result\": \"{\\\"content\\\": ...}\"}` double-JSON; parser returns 0 for these cases. The data is there but path-dependent.\n\n### Cross-session retrieval \u2014 CONFIRMED\nThe June 16 session (`ses_130e4d`) retrieved entries dated **June 1 through June 16**:\n- June 1: \"HADDOCK3 OOM kill on Azzurra\", \"Template for setting up 4 peptide docking\"\n- June 3: \"Peptide construction method and force field CORRECTED\"\n- June 5: \"Always use max walltime for cpucourt\", \"Contact labels are residue categories not interactions\"\n- June 11: \"Always superimpose docked poses before comparing scores\"\n- June 12: \"AIR-free score correct formula and recurring calculation error\"\n- June 13: \"BindCraft jobs on external cluster not tracked by Magnolia\"\n- June 16: \"4PO2 is recommended closed-state receptor\", \"Full HADDOCK3 protocol requires mdref\"\n\n**Conclusion**: Entries created up to 15 days earlier are retrieved in later sessions.\n\n---\n\n## 3. `memory_search` \u2014 31 calls\n\n### Result breakdown\n| Result count | Calls | % |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 results | 13 | 42% |\n| 1 result | 8 | 26% |\n| 2 results | 3 | 10% |\n| 9 results | 1 | 3% |\n| 16 results | 1 | 3% |\n| Unknown | 5 | 16% |\n\n### Zero-result queries (the \"miss\" rate)\nThese searches returned nothing despite staging/entries containing relevant content:\n- `\"bindcraft\"` \u2014 searched 3 times across different sessions, always 0 results\n- `\"KFERQ KILDQ RKDLQ RKELQ QRKEL peptide origin literature CMA substrate\"` \u2014 0 results\n- `\"memory 32GB 64GB submit_job haddock3 OOM resource\"` \u2014 0 results (despite archive entry \"HADDOCK3_OOM_kill_on_Azzurra_32_concurrent_CNS_jobs_exceed_3.md\")\n- `\"peptide construction tleap force field haddock3\"` \u2014 0 results (despite \"Peptide_construction_method_and_force_field_CORRECTED.md\")\n- `\"14-mer\"` \u2014 0 results (despite 14-mer entries)\n- `\"alanine mutation scanning\"` \u2014 0 results\n\n### Successful queries\n- `\"TGFMALQ\"` \u2192 16 results (staging tier, with proper titles!)\n- `\"TGFMALQ 6-mer Hsc70 SBD AIR-free score\"` \u2192 1 result (session-only)\n- `\"BindCraft installation Azzurra miniconda\"` \u2192 1 result\n- `\"HADDOCK3 2GB core memory Azzurra\"` \u2192 1 result\n- `\"RKALQ D3 ALA mutation best 5-mer\"` \u2192 2 results\n- `\"experimentalist\"` \u2192 2 results\n\n### Key observation about memory_search results\nThe search results have **inconsistent structure**:\n- Some have empty `title`, `entry_type`, `tags` fields (session-event raw data)\n- Others (from staging/project tier) have populated `title`, `name`, `path`, `tier`, `tags`\n- The agent explicitly noted this: *\"memory_search \u2014 still session-only (self-referential)\"* then after a broader query: *\"Now it reaches staging. 13 hits\"*\n\n---\n\n## 4. `memory_select_relevant` \u2014 2 calls, both with 0 content\n\nBoth calls returned empty content. This feature appears non-functional in the hsc70 project.\n\n---\n\n## 5. `memory_search_errors` \u2014 11 calls across hsc70 sessions\n\nMost are auto-triggered on tool failures. Error messages are empty or unparseable. Only 1 call produced search results (0 results found).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Does the agent ACT on retrieved knowledge?\n\n### YES \u2014 confirmed cases:\n\n**Case A: MM-GBSA methodology reuse** (June 17, `ses_12b819`)\n- `get_context` for \"MM-GBSA per-residue decomposition\" returned entries: \"Combined contact map + MM-GBSA per-residue analysis identifies pharmacophore\", \"AIR-free score correct formula\", \"Structure-guided 1-residue extension from docked KFERQ\"\n- Agent immediately: **\"Good \u2014 I have the methodology from the previous combined analysis. I need to run MM-GBSA per-residue decomposition on the AF3 models\"**\n- This is a clear retrieval \u2192 action chain\n\n**Case B: Perspicacit\u00e9 KB query** (June 17, `ses_12b819`)\n- `get_context` for \"Perspicacit\u00e9 knowledge base TGGFQMALT\" returned entries about the Perspicacit\u00e9 KB, Torielli paper, and BindCraft\n- Agent: tries to query Perspicacit\u00e9 server, runs `curl` commands, checks API\n\n**Case C: TGFMALQ search summarization** (June 19, `ses_120fa9`)\n- `memory_search(\"TGFMALQ\")` \u2192 16 results\n- Agent: builds a summary table from the 13 key TGFMALQ staging entries\n- This is direct retrieval \u2192 tabulation \u2192 presentation to user\n\n**Case D: Error avoidance via retrieved rules** (June 15, `ses_134c7b`)\n- `get_context` + file reads revealed BindCraft was raw-submitted (bypassing `submit_job`)\n- Agent: creates `rules/job_execution.md` codifying the rule, updates `magnolia.md`\n- Subsequent BindCraft submissions use `submit_job` properly\n\n### The \"waterline\" problem:\nThe agent follows **system rules** (rules/*.md) much more consistently than **memory entries**. The rules are loaded at session start and always visible. Memory entries must be retrieved via get_context/search and often come back with 0 or empty results.\n\n### UNUSED retrieved entries:\nMany entries retrieved by `get_context` are never explicitly referenced by the agent. The agent gets 4-7 entry titles in context but only acts on 1-2 of them. The rest are passive context that might inform tone/approach but don't produce explicit traceable actions.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Bugs and Limitations Found\n\n| Issue | Impact | Occurrences |\n|---|---|---|\n| Double-JSON wrapping in `get_context` output | Parser returns 0 content when `output = {\"result\": \"{\\\"content\\\": ...}\"}` | 2 of 16 calls |\n| `memory_search` returns 0 results for queries that match entry content | Agent never sees relevant past learnings | 42% of searches |\n| `memory_search` result fields empty (title, entry_type = \"\") | Agent sees a hit count but no usable information | ~8 calls |\n| `memory_select_relevant` always returns 0 content | Tool non-functional | 2 of 2 calls |\n| `memory_search_errors` has empty error messages | Cannot match current error to past resolutions | Majority |\n| No `memory_get_run_history` usage observed | Agent doesn't use the runs index for context | 0 calls in hsc70 data |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Verdict\n\n**Magnolia stores learnings, and sometimes retrieves and reuses them \u2014 but not always and not consistently.**\n\nThe retrieval pipeline has real bugs (42% search miss rate, empty titles, double-JSON parsing issues). When retrieval works, the agent does act on the knowledge (MM-GBSA methodology, TGFMALQ summary table, BindCraft rule creation). But the system rules (`rules/*.md`) are a much more reliable mechanism for cross-session knowledge transfer than the memory entries.\n\nThe memory system is in its **mid-implementation** state: the storage layer works, the retrieval API exists, but the semantic matching between query and entry content is unreliable, and result formatting is inconsistent.\nREPORT_EOF\n\ncat /tmp/hsc70_retrieval_report.md"}
